You seem to be heading for 'hybrid' mixture models that allow for unknown-sex animals (see ?hcov and secr-finitemixtures.pdf <https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-finitemixtures.pdf>). These are specified with the hcov argument of secr.fit (i.e. hcov = 'sex' where 'sex is a covariate name) AND model = list(lambda0~h2, sigma~h2). Compare a model with hcov='sex' and model=list(lambda0~1, sigma~1). (I'm assuming detectfn = 'HEX'; otherwise swap g0 for lambda0).

