I'm not going to untangle your R data manipulation issue, but note "Missing values (NA) are used for individuals of unknown class. If hcov has more than two levels, all but the first two levels are converted to NA". So because the levels of your factor are 'f', 'm' and 'UID' in that order, UID will automatically be treated as NA, and no pre-processing is needed.

